    description: "Pass 17 finding OOOOOO. All 84 AnalysisRun records have 15 fields: config_fingerprint, duration_ms, execution_id, failed_files, files_analyzed, files_skipped, pass, pass_version, repo_fingerprint, run_signature, skipped_passes, started_at, toolchain, version, warnings. None of: nodes_emitted, edges_emitted, output_size_bytes. To answer 'pyffi-linker emitted how many edges?' one must scan all 108649 edges checking origin lists for 'pyffi-linker'. This makes dead-pass detection (pass 16 NNNNN/OOOOO/PPPPP) a multi-million-element filter operation per query. The data is computable but not curated. Direct fields would also make pass-productivity dashboards trivial."  # e799
    fields:  # e799
      statement: "The AnalysisRun record should expose nodes_emitted and edges_emitted fields directly so consumers can answer 'which pass produced how much output' without scanning the entire nodes/edges lists for matching origins."  # e799
      root_cause: "The AnalysisRun schema records files_analyzed/files_skipped/duration_ms but no production-output counters. Pipeline does not aggregate per-pass emission counts at orchestration time."  # e799
